<title>USA: U.S. April retail sales fell 0.3 percent. [CORRECTED 21:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>U.S. April retail sales fell 0.3 percent. [CORRECTED 21:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on U.S. retail sales.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Apr    Mar-(Prev)  Apr97/96</p>
<p> Retail Sales	   -0.3    UNCH  0.1     4.9</p>
<p> Excluding Autos	-0.1    0.1   0.5     4.2</p>
<p> Auto Sales	     -0.9   -0.3  -1.1     7.0</p>
<p> Durable Goods	  -0.5   -0.3  -0.2     6.8</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods     -0.3    0.2   0.4     3.6</p>
<p> Furniture Stores     -0.3   -1.1   0.1     2.8</p>
<p> Building Materials    UNCH   1.0   1.5     8.8</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Apr     Mar-(Previous)    Feb--(Prev)</p>
<p> Retail Sales	 212.24   212.97  213.63   213.02  213.39</p>
<p> Excluding Autos    160.38   160.61  161.22   160.48  160.38</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    51.86    52.36   52.42    52.54   53.01</p>
<p> Durable Goods	 87.09    87.50   87.98    87.79   88.19</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods   125.15   125.47  125.65   125.24  125.20</p>
<p> Furniture Stores    11.43    11.46   11.64    11.59   11.63</p>
<p> Building Materials  12.02    12.02   11.96    11.90   11.79</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Apr    Mar-(Prev)  Apr97/96</p>
<p> General Merch.Stores -0.9   -0.1   0.5     4.4</p>
<p> Department Stores    -1.0    0.1   0.7     5.0</p>
<p> Food Stores	    -0.5    0.6   0.4     2.2</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	 -0.5    0.6   0.5     1.7</p>
<p> Gas Stations	   -0.1   -0.5  -0.7     1.6</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 -0.6   -1.0   1.1    -0.1</p>
