<p> Eat/Drink Places	0.5    0.2  UNCH     4.9</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    -0.1    0.7   0.8     9.7</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Apr     Mar-(Previous)     Feb----(Prev)</p>
<p> Gen.Merch.Stores    27.23    27.49    27.71     27.51   27.58</p>
<p> Department Stores   21.42    21.63    21.82     21.60   21.66</p>
<p> Food Stores	   35.88    36.06    36.07     35.84   35.92</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	33.79    33.97    34.04     33.78   33.85</p>
<p> Gas Stations	  13.26    13.28    13.20     13.35   13.29</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 9.56     9.62     9.81	9.71    9.71</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places    20.60    20.50    20.31     20.47   20.31</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    8.13     8.14     8.11	8.08    8.05</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected April retail sales to fall 0.3 percent, and sales excluding autos to be up 0.1 percent.</p>
<p>The 0.3 percent drop in April retail sales was the first decline of the year and the largest since a 0.5 percent drop last June, the department said.</p>
<p>It revised February retail sales to a 1.3 percent increase from a 1.5 percent rise. It revised February sales excluding autos to a 0.8 percent rise from up 0.7 percent, and February auto sales to up 2.9 percent from a 3.9 percent rise.</p>
<p>The department revised U.S. March retail sales data in its annual benchmark revisions issued May 2.</p>
